    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43-a1">

                <pb facs="0459" n="449" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv05/pg449"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Annex] A</seg></opener>
                <head>[<hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Supreme Council</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hankey</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary General of the Peace Conference</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Dutasta</hi>)]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-03">3 <hi rendition="#small-caps">May</hi>,
                        1919</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Colleague</hi>, At a Meeting held this
                    morning between President Wilson, Mr. Lloyd George and M. Loucheur, with
                    financial experts, it was decided that the Financial Chapter should be brought
                    into accordance with the provision in the Chapter on Belgium, to the effect that
                    Government property in German territory ceded to Belgium should be transferred,
                    without the obligation on the part of Belgium of making any payment or credit in
                    favour of Germany.</p>
                <p>It is suggested therefore, that in Clause 9 of the Financial Chapter, the
                    following words should be added to the last paragraph:— <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Belgium shall also be exempt from making any payment or credit under
                            this Clause for any property or possessions of the German Empire or
                            States situated in German territory ceded to Belgium under this
                            Treaty.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <pb facs="0460" n="450" xml:id="pg450"/>
                <p>I am directed to request that your Excellency will forward this letter as soon as
                    possible to the Drafting Committee.</p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. P. A. Hankey</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
